- op: discuss  # db96
  at: '2026-09-19T05:15:54Z'  # db96
  by: agent  # db96
  actor: jgstern_agent  # db96
  clock: 6  # db96
  nonce: db96  # db96
  message: "DONE (PR in pr_ref). Row 6 of the owner-authorised sequence. Rulings 1, 4, 6 and 13 of ADR-0057.\n\nWHAT LANDED. (§6) Symbol and Edge gain `attribution: {field: [pass_id, ...]}` (who holds the value the scalar slot carries: both producers on agreement, the arbitration winner on a contest, the sole observer otherwise) and `alternatives: {field: [{value, origin: [pass_id, ...]}]}` (present only for contested fields — nothing a producer emitted is discarded, §1). Dict-valued, so no `# axis:` line (keys are field names, leaves pass ids); emitted by to_dict only when set and read by from_dict; declared conditional in generate_schema_lib with sample population; docs/schema.json regenerated; SCHEMA_VERSION 0.20.10 -> 0.20.11 (additive; a single-producer artifact is byte-identical). (§4) merge_producers.arbitrate(candidates, precedence): pure over the candidate set, precedence = incumbent_first order (the §5 built-in until WI-hukuf), `span` decided by the item-role member instead; _stamp_slot arbitrates every tracked attribute, sets the scalar and writes attribution/alternatives in one step — the pass no longer copies the incumbent. (§13) `corroborated` joins VALID_CONFIDENCE_SOURCES (ir.py + spec_validator's bounded enum + schema decoration); CORROBORATED_CONFIDENCE = 0.95 declared in merge_producers; CONFIDENCE_MODEL hypergumbo-evidence-v2.0 -> v2.1 (spec Appendix C note; two tests re-pinned). The merge pass now FOLDS the participants' agreeing edges itself (§11) — incumbent-first survivor, others' call sites absorbed via _absorb_call_site, origin union, edge_key reset, origin_run_id = the producer-merge run — rather than leaving them to deduplicate_edges, whose survivor is encounter order and the SCIP arm runs first by priority. Two distinct evidence pathways on one (src, dst, edge_type) -> confidence 0.95, confidence_source corroborated, attribution.confidence = both producers, alternatives.confidence = each original; the same pathway twice keeps the incumbent's value and source. finalize's re-derivation leaves any source other than evidence_derived alone, so corroborated survives to the artifact.\n\nEVIDENCE on committed input (test_recorded_fixtures.py): all 148 merged records carry the slot; span contested on 146 (the 2 unit enum variants agree — tree-sitter spans the bare name), stable_id contested on 134 (14 single-line items already reach rust.py's id through the parity helper, INV-dolud's one case), kind contested on the 15 const items with alternatives [{constant, [rust_analyzer]}]; the 93 shared call keys become 93 corroborated edges at 0.95 (attribution [rust, rust_analyzer], both originals in alternatives, incumbent evidence_type kept), 149 edges absorbed in total (121 SCIP twins + each arm's own repeats, lines unioned); no single-producer record carries the slot. Pipeline (test_merge_pass_in_pipeline.py): the artifact JSON carries attribution/alternatives on the two merged nodes only, kind contested on `Alias` (type_alias vs the incumbent's variable), schema_version 0.20.11. 11 unit tests on the slot and the fold (contest, agreement, disjoint coverage, token-span alternative, no slot on a single producer, round trip both directions; corroboration, same-pathway precedence, lonely edge untouched, edge-only fold still records the run). Mutation: disabling the distinct-pathway test turns 3 tests red.\n\nNOT ASSERTED. The slot is on Symbol and Edge only (no AnalysisRun / usage-context provenance). Arbitration precedence is still the inferred incumbent order (registry.ALTERNATIVE_BACKENDS), not a config preference — WI-hukuf. The acceptance clause \"the 52 free functions show kind alternatives from both producers until the SCIP kind fix lands\" is moot: WI-gapup landed first, so they agree."  # db96
